-- #1641 — NOT GRADED BY THIS GATE (it cannot be: see below). This is main.mdk with the
-- constraint wrapper removed from the first impl head and NOTHING else changed —
-- `impl Zero Int` instead of `impl Zero (Eq x => Int)`. It is the one-dimension comparison
-- the whole issue rests on, and it is CORRECTLY REJECTED:
--
--   check -> exit 1, on the `zero` occurrence in `main`:
--     Ambiguous instance for `Zero`. Cannot determine which impl; add a type annotation
--   run -> exit 1, same diagnostic;  build -> exit 1, same diagnostic
--
-- (measured first-hand 2026-08-15. The message is the observable; no line:col is quoted
-- here on purpose, since editing this comment block would move it.)
--
-- ⚠️ WHY IT IS NOT THE GRADED CONTROL. This harness defines a control as a near-identical
-- program that must stay GREEN, and enforces that by requiring EXIT 0. Here the control
-- shape is the program that is correctly REFUSED — the subject is the one wrongly accepted
-- — so the usual polarity is inverted and the harness cannot express it: posing this file
-- as `control:` would report CONTROL-BROKE on a healthy tree on every single run. The
-- graded control is control.mdk; this file is evidence, and the comparison it makes is
-- recorded in claim.txt rather than asserted mechanically.
interface Zero a where
  zero : a

impl Zero Int where
  zero = 0

impl Zero Bool where
  zero = False

ignore2 : a -> Int
ignore2 _ = 5

main = println (ignore2 zero)
